<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">6 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 6 November, from 1860 to 1962.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1860 CE <span class="tih-ago">166 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abraham Lincoln is elected president</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Abraham Lincoln won the presidency with under 40 per cent of the popular vote, carrying only northern states. His victory prompted South Carolina to secede within weeks, followed by six more states.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1869 CE <span class="tih-ago">157 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Rutgers and Princeton play the first college football game</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Rutgers beat Princeton 6-4 in New Brunswick, New Jersey, in the first intercollegiate football match. The rules resembled soccer more than modern American football.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/south-africa.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1913 CE <span class="tih-ago">113 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Gandhi is arrested leading a march of Indian miners</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In South Africa, Gandhi was arrested at Palmford while leading over 2,000 striking Indian workers across the Transvaal border in defiance of discriminatory laws. The campaign won concessions in 1914.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1917 CE <span class="tih-ago">109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Canadian troops capture Passchendaele</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Canadian forces took the ruined village of Passchendaele, ending the Third Battle of Ypres. The British-led offensive had gained a few miles of Flemish mud at a cost of hundreds of thousands of casualties.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1962 CE <span class="tih-ago">64 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The UN General Assembly calls for sanctions on South Africa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Resolution 1761 condemned apartheid and urged member states to break diplomatic ties and boycott South African trade. It also set up a special committee against apartheid.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a></div></div></li></ol>
